- op: discuss  # bbd5
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:00Z'  # bbd5
  by: agent  # bbd5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bbd5
  clock: 3  # bbd5
  nonce: bbd5  # bbd5
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE and too narrow. Title updated.\n- net/http.NewRequest is NO LONGER A ROW: removed by 6b8e27c00f (PR #1188, INV-gujoh family; INV-gujoh satisfied, and its A/B showed the flow still reaches Client.Do). The loader returns [] for NewRequest and NewRequestWithContext.\n- Still rowed subprocess: go.yaml:382-383 os/exec [Command, CommandContext, LookPath], and the overlay io_primitives_overlays/go-x-sys-and-grpc.yaml:83 repeats them for golang.org/x/sys/execabs (not in this item). Repro: os.Getenv feeding exec.LookPath(name) and exec.CommandContext(ctx, name), nothing ever run. Both appear as subprocess; host_secret->subprocess and \"never launches a subprocess\" read violated.\n- SCOPE: CommandContext cannot be decided without Command (CommandContext only calls Command; Command only builds a *Cmd). Same shape: rust Command::new (rust.yaml:342) and java ProcessBuilder.command (java.yaml:186, a setter).\n- FIX SPLITS: LookPath (+execabs) can be deleted on its own; it launches nothing. Command/CommandContext fall under ADR-0049 Ruling 3: the constructor's arguments are the only carrier of the sink data and Cmd.Run/Start take none, so removing them needs a represented crossing (taint through the *Cmd receiver into Run/Start/Output) measured at the finding level, as NewRequest needed WI-jikik first. Tests pinning os/exec.Command as subprocess/high-risk: test_io_boundary.py:507 and :2909. Not the one-line row fix the 10-02 triage called it.\n- NOT CHECKED: whether taint already propagates from a *Cmd receiver into Cmd.Run."  # bbd5
- op: discuss  # b3d6
  at: '2026-10-03T13:17:41Z'  # b3d6
  by: agent  # b3d6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b3d6
  clock: 4  # b3d6
  nonce: b3d6  # b3d6
  message: "DEPENDENCY NOTE FROM WI-kozaj (2026-10-03). The owner's sequencing named WI-kozaj's return-type mechanism as a dependency of this item's Command half. Checked: for GO it already exists and is not what blocks this item. library_signatures/go.yaml has shipped `exec.Command: exec.Cmd` and `exec.CommandContext: exec.Cmd` since WI-lalot, and test_library_signatures.py::test_go_types_the_subprocess_producer_INV_muhij_named pins `c := exec.Command(...); c.Start()` emitting go:os/exec.Cmd:0-0:Start. WI-kozaj's new mechanism is the PYTHON consumer of the same family (py.py _library_producer_type). The difference from csv: csv's data enters at the EXECUTOR (w.writerow(row)), so typing the receiver is enough to relocate the crossing. exec.Command's data (the argv) enters at the CONSTRUCTOR and Cmd.Run / Start take none, so relocating that row needs taint carried from the constructor's arguments through the *Cmd receiver into Run/Start -- an object-carries-its-arguments propagation, not a return type. NOT CHECKED: whether that propagation already happens (the 10-03 premise audit also left it unchecked)."  # b3d6
