  nonce: 2d77  # 2d77
  message: "Merged in PR #1417 (dev c5249c1aa1).\n\nLookPath half fixed on jgstern-agent/fix/mulul-catalogue-rows (e94b1aace0): os/exec.LookPath and the community golang.org/x/sys/execabs.LookPath moved subprocess -> fs_read (python shutil.which parity); their high-risk exemptions removed. Behavioral evidence: a go fixture calling exec.LookPath(os.Getenv(\"TOOL\")) and launching nothing now CONFIRMS \"never launches a subprocess\" and host_secret->subprocess (before: both violated, and four other claims carried an opaque_boundary caveat). Corpus io-boundaries A/B: docker-compose 1 and runc 3 LookPath chains moved subprocess -> fs_read, no other boundary count changed. ITEM STAYS OPEN: os/exec Command / CommandContext (and the execabs twins) remain subprocess by design until taint is represented through the *Cmd receiver into Run/Start/Output (ADR-0049 ruling 3, WI-kozaj); a control test pins them.\n\nINTEGRATOR CORRECTION: the dependency on WI-kozaj recorded above and in the 10-03 sequence is wrong. WI-kozaj (PR #1417) added a Python library-signature return type; Go already types exec.Command's result as exec.Cmd. What this half needs is taint carried from the constructor's ARGUMENTS through the *Cmd receiver into Run/Start/Output (stage 4)."  # 2d77
- op: discuss  # bbb5
