  nonce: bbb5  # bbb5
  message: "WI-vafad tranche 3 (2026-10-03, docs/audits/0022 T3-H2) found the SCALA TWIN of this item's Command half. scala.yaml rows `scala.sys.process.Process` [apply, Process] (+ [run]) under subprocess, and every apply overload only RETURNS a ProcessBuilder (scala/src/library/scala/sys/process/Process.scala:57-102); the launch is run / ! / !!. It is the same builder-under-subprocess shape as go os/exec Command/CommandContext, with the same blocker: the builder's arguments are the only carrier of argv, so moving it needs taint through the builder receiver first (go.yaml:396-403). Both blind MIX2 workers proposed NONE. The verifier HELD it for this item's mechanism rather than filing it alone. The fs_write `simultaneous` half of the same scala row is a separate, unblocked removal: filed as WI-novap-tugaz-bovag-lobid-radok-gibov-sibog-zujut."  # bbb5
- op: discuss  # 4bf4
  at: '2026-10-03T21:39:27Z'  # 4bf4
  by: agent  # 4bf4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4bf4
  clock: 8  # 4bf4
  nonce: 4bf4  # 4bf4
  message: "kanor run 2026-10-03, Command/CommandContext half: MEASURED, BLOCKED, no row moved. Branch jgstern-agent/fix/kanor, commit a8e8fd09fd (docs + pin only).\n\nTHE ASKED PROPAGATION ALREADY EXISTS. With os/exec.{Command,CommandContext} (and the execabs twins) removed in a probe arm, the DDG carries the argv into `cmd` and `cmd.Run()` uses it: the same-scope fixture reads violated at os/exec.Cmd.Run, ddg CONFIRMED (with the row it is ddg_mixed/escaped, because INV-fumod's no-inheritance-across-an-I/O-name rule fires on the row itself). Same for chained .CombinedOutput(), .Output(), cmd passed to a callee, CommandContext + Start, cmd.Env = append(..secret).\n\nRULING 3 FAILS AT THE FINDING LEVEL. Fixtures violated -> inconclusive (finding lost): a factory returning *exec.Cmd; a *Cmd stored in a struct field and started by another method; execabs.Command(x).Run() (no library signature, untyped). Also every clean Go program calling exec.Command goes confirmed_with_caveats -> inconclusive (os/exec becomes an unclassified module); a completeness entry would cure that but turn the three lost shapes into FALSE CLEANS.\nCorpus (docker-compose, runc, containers-storage, buildah, ingress-nginx; generic taint claims + host-secret-no-subprocess): 0 verdicts moved; 15 flows removed: 12 are a command's own output paired with its constructor (false positives, rightly removed), 1 buildah os.Stdin wiring, and 2 REAL flows lost -- runc Container.newParentProcess (os.Getenv(\"GOMAXPROCS\") into cmd.Env, Start in another method) and buildah unshareCmd ($SHELL into a Cmd run by unshare.ExecRunnable). 1 precise -> approximate (containers-storage unshareFn: field store + if-initializer). Site census: 17 of 318 non-test constructor sites (5.3%) have no executor reachable forward from their function (factories).\n\nBLOCKERS FILED: INV-komoj (a source returned to a caller is never followed; a false clean on the plain helper idiom today), WI-jahip (a field store kills the receiver's reaching definition). Also needed before a move: an execabs.Command library signature, the os/exec completeness decision, and a story for a Cmd run by a library function. Same shape, NOT measured: rust Command::new, java ProcessBuilder.command.\nCHANGED: go.yaml note (it named WI-kozaj, the wrong dependency); test_go_lookpath_is_not_a_launch.py control renamed + new pin test_a_factory_returned_cmd_is_still_caught_at_its_constructor (reads inconclusive, i.e. fails, with the rows removed); ADR-0049 implementation state. Report: decontend/run_10032026/kanor.md."  # 4bf4
