  clock: 11  # 5bec
  nonce: 5bec  # 5bec
  message: "2026-10-05, INV-komoj run (branch jgstern-agent/fix/komoj): kanor's Command-half measurement re-run on this branch. The os/exec Command/CommandContext rows and the execabs overlay rows were removed in a scratch copy, not committed.\n\nFixtures (kanor gofx, arm without rows):\n- g2_return (a factory returns *exec.Cmd): base inconclusive -> komoj VIOLATED, ddg confirmed at Cmd.Run. The return lift closes the factory blocker.\n- Unchanged: g6_field (Cmd stored in a struct field, Start in another method) inconclusive; g8_execabs inconclusive; c1_clean inconclusive (os/exec unclassified); c2_unrun inconclusive.\n\nCorpus:\n- runc newParentProcess (GOMAXPROCS -> cmd.Env): the source is now lifted into Container.start and above, and still reaches the subprocess zone. BUT the only witness sink is configs.Command.Run's Cmd.Start, i.e. the hooks' Cmd. The real executor, p.cmd.Start() in initProcess.start / setnsProcess.start, has a struct-field receiver, is not typed os/exec.Cmd, and is no sink at all (the g6 shape). So the real flow is NOT represented.\n- buildah unshareCmd ($SHELL): still lost. The Cmd goes to the vendored unshare.ExecRunnable(cmd Runnable, ..), which calls Run on an interface; no return is involved.\n- Removing the rows moves no verdict on runc or buildah, in either arm.\n\nConclusion: the Command half still cannot proceed. INV-komoj removes the factory-return blocker only. Still blocking: a struct-field *Cmd receiver (runc's real executor), a Cmd run through an interface by a library function, execabs, and the os/exec completeness decision.\n\nArtifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/komoj/vc/{A,Adukam,B,Bdukam}.{runc,buildah}.*; report run_10032026/komoj.md §5."  # 5bec
